  securityToken?: string(name='SecurityToken'),
  timeShift?: string(name='TimeShift', description='When you restore a classic architecture instance, you can apply an offset to the expiration time of keys regardless of whether you choose to restore full data or specified keys. Specify the time in the yyyy-MM-ddTHH:mmZ format. The time must be in UTC. The instance calculates the remaining expiration duration of the keys at the specified flashback point in time, starting from the specified expiration offset point in time.
> * This feature supports offsetting the expiration time only at the key level. It does not support offsetting the internal expiration time of keys in Tair-developed data structures, such as the fields in exHash and the skeys in TS.
